# Build context for the official Linux/RunPod experiment image.
#
# DENY BY DEFAULT, then re-include exactly what the runtime needs. An allow-list is used on purpose:
# a deny-list silently ships whatever it forgets, and this repository sits next to datasets,
# checkpoints and a protected reference PDF.

**

# ---- source the runtime actually imports ----
!src/**
!configs/**
!scripts/**

# ---- environment specifications ----
!requirements-runpod.lock
!requirements-runpod.in
!requirements.lock
!requirements-e1.txt

# ---- teacher image (Dockerfile.teacher) ----
# The deny-by-default `**` above excludes these from the build context, so `COPY
# requirements-teacher.lock ./` cannot see the file and the teacher build fails at that layer.
# Dockerfile.teacher itself is re-included too: BuildKit transfers the `-f` file through a separate
# context so this is probably redundant, but "probably" is not a property worth relying on for one
# line. Neither file is copied into the E1 image, which names its inputs explicitly.
!requirements-teacher.lock
!Dockerfile.teacher

# ---- the only docs read at runtime (src/eval/artifacts.py, src/stats/artifact.py) ----
!docs/IMPLEMENTATION_CONTRACT.md
!docs/EVALUATION_CONTRACT.md
!docs/STATISTICAL_ANALYSIS_CONTRACT.md

# ---- re-exclusions that must win regardless of the allow-list above ----
# PROTECTED: never copy, read or hash the reference PDF.
docs/reference/**
# datasets and model artifacts stay outside the image (mounted at run time)
data/**
datasets/**
plantseg_data/**
weights/**
outputs/**
**/*.pt
**/*.pth
**/*.ckpt
**/*.onnx
**/*.zip
**/*.tar
**/*.tar.gz
**/*.7z
**/*.rar
# secrets / credentials / keys
**/.env
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/id_rsa*
**/id_ed25519*
**/.ssh/**
**/.netrc
**/.aws/**
**/*credentials*
**/*secret*
# build noise
**/__pycache__/**
**/*.pyc
.git/**
.github/**
reports/**

# ---- LAST WORD: the one reports/ file the runtime hard-depends on ----
# .dockerignore is LAST-MATCH-WINS, so this MUST stay below `reports/**` or it is overridden.
# Not a report: the B18a CE class-weight vector loaded by train_e1.py:49,55,293 through a fail-closed
# loader. Re-included by exact path so the rest of reports/ stays out of the image.
!reports/e1_class_weights.json
